  {
    "sha": "27b7f137bc7c46dc6ddfa624800b5b47a8c14955",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOUOlySdoAKDI3YjdmMTM3YmM3YzQ2ZGM2ZGRmYTYyNDgwMGI1YjQ3YThjMTQ5NTU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "fernandomunozgarza",
        "email": "fer.munoz2012@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-10-27T06:36:23Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "fernandomunozgarza",
        "email": "fer.munoz2012@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-10-27T06:36:23Z"
      },
      "message": "Keep Excel check-in times from shifting by the timezone\n\nThe customer's attendance file is xlsx and its Checked In column is a real Excel date, not text. Wehen read, the library returns its value in UTC, so parser converted it into Central and moved it back five hours. 10:33 PM becomes 5:33 PM.\n\nExcel dates have no timezone, so the fix reads the date and time exactly as written and stores that, so 10 PM stays 10 PM. It also makes an xlsx and csv row of the same time store the same checked_in_at. Adds the sample file given by customer as a test file and covers it in parser, mapper, and upload specs.",
